00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.173
- So one of the questions
I get asked a lot

00:00:26.173 --> 00:00:27.960
from entrepreneurs is
how do I stay positive?

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.248
How do I avoid going
into the negative zone?

00:00:30.248 --> 00:00:31.900
You know, as an entrepreneur,

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.156
it's really hard to get my business going.

00:00:33.156 --> 00:00:34.516
There's so many pains and struggles,

00:00:34.516 --> 00:00:35.727
and people don't believe in me,

00:00:35.727 --> 00:00:36.943
and I'm always being told to quit

00:00:36.943 --> 00:00:38.193
and go do the safe, smart
thing and get a job.

00:00:38.193 --> 00:00:39.856
How do I stay positive?

00:00:39.856 --> 00:00:41.377
How do I stay out of
that negative territory?

00:00:41.377 --> 00:00:43.192
And so today, I'm going to share with you

00:00:43.192 --> 00:00:46.315
my seven ways on how to
avoid negative thinking.

00:00:46.315 --> 00:00:48.453
And it's a little bit of
background on myself, too.

00:00:48.453 --> 00:00:50.722
I'm currently going through
this in the micro way.

00:00:50.722 --> 00:00:52.149
One of the things that
I've challenged myself

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:55.898
is to restructure my thinking around

00:00:55.898 --> 00:00:57.857
there is no such thing as a bad day.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.380
I'm trying to really embody that.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:00.986
There is no such thing as a bad day,

00:01:00.986 --> 00:01:02.669
and I'm going to share with you

00:01:02.669 --> 00:01:05.573
how I'm fixing that, how
I'm believing in that,

00:01:05.573 --> 00:01:07.325
that will hopefully
help you along your path

00:01:07.325 --> 00:01:09.110
to avoid your negative thinking as well.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.693
(upbeat music)

00:01:12.695 --> 00:01:14.383
So step number one is catching yourself.

00:01:14.383 --> 00:01:15.997
This is honestly one of the hardest parts.

00:01:15.997 --> 00:01:17.615
We don't even know when
we're being negative.

00:01:17.615 --> 00:01:18.854
It's just default.

00:01:18.854 --> 00:01:20.026
We're on autopilot mode.

00:01:20.026 --> 00:01:21.817
We're constantly just in survival mode,

00:01:21.817 --> 00:01:23.089
just trying to put out fires.

00:01:23.089 --> 00:01:25.449
And we don't even catch
the negative thoughts

00:01:25.449 --> 00:01:27.240
that we have, we just feel them.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.083
And I think that's the
first, biggest challenge

00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:31.278
is being able to step outside,

00:01:31.278 --> 00:01:33.590
whether that's you,
yourself examining your day,

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.704
whether you, in the morning, ask yourself

00:01:35.704 --> 00:01:37.683
how you're feeling, or
how you felt yesterday,

00:01:37.683 --> 00:01:39.228
or taking a break at lunch,

00:01:39.228 --> 00:01:40.741
or taking a break in the afternoon,

00:01:40.741 --> 00:01:42.446
or at the evening, reflecting back.

00:01:42.446 --> 00:01:44.001
A lot of people, a lot of entrepreneurs

00:01:44.001 --> 00:01:45.261
use journals to kind of think about

00:01:45.261 --> 00:01:46.365
how the day has gone,

00:01:46.365 --> 00:01:47.620
and just reflect.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:49.071
Like, was I negative today?

00:01:49.071 --> 00:01:50.604
Did I have negative thoughts?

00:01:50.604 --> 00:01:52.869
Was I being positive today, right?

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:55.022
Like any goal that you have,

00:01:55.022 --> 00:01:57.310
the more that you can
track it and measure it,

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:59.149
the more likely you're going
to make progress on it.

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:00.374
So what's your method of tracking

00:02:00.374 --> 00:02:03.017
whether you had a negative day or not?

00:02:03.017 --> 00:02:04.805
Because if you cannot catch yourself

00:02:04.805 --> 00:02:06.734
in the moment of being negative,

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:09.470
then it's going to be hard for
you to change that behavior.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:10.815
So whether it's journaling,

00:02:10.815 --> 00:02:13.817
whether it's taking time
out at specific parts

00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:15.164
to see if you're being negative,

00:02:15.164 --> 00:02:16.685
whether it's working with somebody

00:02:16.685 --> 00:02:18.721
and saying, hey, if you
catch me being negative,

00:02:18.721 --> 00:02:19.777
let me know.

00:02:19.777 --> 00:02:21.847
Having some kind of form of checking

00:02:21.847 --> 00:02:24.451
so that you're not just
always in autopilot mode

00:02:24.451 --> 00:02:26.273
and you know exactly when
you're being negative,

00:02:26.273 --> 00:02:28.997
when you figure that out,
you can start fixing it.

00:02:28.997 --> 00:02:31.580
(upbeat music)

00:02:32.454 --> 00:02:34.132
Step number two is turn
your negative statements

00:02:34.132 --> 00:02:35.855
into how questions.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.188
This is one of my favorite exercises.

00:02:37.188 --> 00:02:38.921
If there's a negative
thought that you have,

00:02:38.921 --> 00:02:41.935
something that, you just
can't do this because,

00:02:41.935 --> 00:02:43.399
or you're so upset because,

00:02:43.399 --> 00:02:44.889
turn it into a how question.

00:02:44.889 --> 00:02:46.968
Turn it into a how can I.

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:49.394
Or turn it into a gratitude statement.

00:02:49.394 --> 00:02:52.000
So as an example, if you are upset that

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.873
somebody's off and had some major success

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.535
and you ready about their bio,

00:02:55.535 --> 00:02:57.180
and they had the same ideas you did,

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.724
and, you know, they went
to Harvard and you didn't,

00:02:59.724 --> 00:03:02.052
you blame it on, you know,
not going to university,

00:03:02.052 --> 00:03:03.224
then you can ask yourself,

00:03:03.224 --> 00:03:05.306
instead of just complaining
about, being negative,

00:03:05.306 --> 00:03:07.263
turn into a how question.

00:03:07.263 --> 00:03:09.570
How can I succeed despite
not going to Harvard?

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:12.763
How can I succeed despite
not having the education,

00:03:12.763 --> 00:03:14.674
or the money, or the right parents,

00:03:14.674 --> 00:03:16.519
or the right connections?

00:03:16.519 --> 00:03:18.462
Whatever it is that you're
blaming the world on, right?

00:03:18.462 --> 00:03:19.867
How can I succeed despite.

00:03:19.867 --> 00:03:23.463
Asking that how to question
takes your negative situation

00:03:23.463 --> 00:03:25.640
and turns it into something positive.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.899
The resource-less into
the resourceful, right?

00:03:28.899 --> 00:03:30.824
We're thinking about how do
we make this amazing thing

00:03:30.824 --> 00:03:33.501
happen now out of this negative situation.

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.600
So as long as you're
staying in this negative,

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.550
down situation, all these limited beliefs,

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.590
you're going to stay there.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:39.876
You're going to stay
in the negative state.

00:03:39.876 --> 00:03:41.010
But if you start asking yourself

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.086
how do I solve it,

00:03:42.086 --> 00:03:44.781
you're forcing your brain
to think in a positive way.

00:03:44.781 --> 00:03:46.115
You're forcing your
brain to solve a problem,

00:03:46.115 --> 00:03:47.493
and when you do that,

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.185
you move to a world of opportunity.

00:03:49.185 --> 00:03:50.542
The gratitude side of things is

00:03:50.542 --> 00:03:53.194
maybe you're upset about, you know,

00:03:53.194 --> 00:03:55.069
the elevator being late, you know?

00:03:55.069 --> 00:03:56.708
I'm stuck in this elevator,

00:03:56.708 --> 00:03:58.812
and I'm waiting forever
for this elevator to come,

00:03:58.812 --> 00:04:00.066
or you're stuck in traffic,

00:04:00.066 --> 00:04:01.639
or there's something that's
outside your control.

00:04:01.639 --> 00:04:03.072
For me the thing that really helps

00:04:03.072 --> 00:04:05.813
is just thinking about gratitude.

00:04:05.813 --> 00:04:08.059
So turn your expectations
into appreciation.

00:04:08.059 --> 00:04:10.323
So, you know, it's pretty impressive

00:04:10.323 --> 00:04:11.733
that there's this magical box

00:04:11.733 --> 00:04:13.483
that will take me from the ground floor

00:04:13.483 --> 00:04:16.211
to the 20th floor, and I
don't have to walk the stairs.

00:04:16.211 --> 00:04:18.791
And, yeah, I have to
wait an extra 45 seconds

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.883
for it to come, but it's
not the end of the world.

00:04:20.883 --> 00:04:22.693
So just shifting perspective, again,

00:04:22.693 --> 00:04:24.343
it starts with catching.

00:04:24.343 --> 00:04:25.425
You got to catch it.

00:04:25.425 --> 00:04:26.558
You got to catch when
you're being negative.

00:04:26.558 --> 00:04:27.516
If you can't catch it,

00:04:27.516 --> 00:04:28.989
you're not going to fix it.

00:04:28.989 --> 00:04:30.748
If you catch it, then turn
it into a how to question

00:04:30.748 --> 00:04:33.386
or just showing appreciation and gratitude

00:04:33.386 --> 00:04:34.960
instead of false expectations

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.225
can really help reframe the situation.

00:04:37.225 --> 00:04:39.808
(upbeat music)

00:04:40.689 --> 00:04:42.389
Step number three is create
a better environment.

00:04:42.389 --> 00:04:45.602
One of my go-tos, always,
when you're trying

00:04:45.602 --> 00:04:47.576
to change a habit, when you're
trying to change something

00:04:47.576 --> 00:04:49.647
that is, subconsciously,
you're always doing,

00:04:49.647 --> 00:04:53.165
is to make it part of your
habit and your daily routines.

00:04:53.165 --> 00:04:55.258
And so if you're trying
to avoid being negative,

00:04:55.258 --> 00:04:57.965
then think about, okay, what's
negative that's in your life.

00:04:57.965 --> 00:05:00.692
You know, are there negative
people that are in your life?

00:05:00.692 --> 00:05:02.382
Can you try not to be around them

00:05:02.382 --> 00:05:03.217
on a daily basis?

00:05:03.217 --> 00:05:05.256
How can you then bring more positivity

00:05:05.256 --> 00:05:07.002
into your life on a consistent basis?

00:05:07.002 --> 00:05:08.129
What are your morning routines?

00:05:08.129 --> 00:05:10.170
Part of what I do every
day is I remind myself,

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.004
I'm trying to work on that
there is no such thing

00:05:12.004 --> 00:05:13.401
as a bad day, right?

00:05:13.401 --> 00:05:14.919
So I remind myself every day,

00:05:14.919 --> 00:05:17.071
one of the things I believe
is no such thing as a bad day.

00:05:17.071 --> 00:05:19.249
Try to remember, try to
feel it, yes, and remember,

00:05:19.249 --> 00:05:21.259
there's something that is important to me.

00:05:21.259 --> 00:05:23.360
It's back on my radar again.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.211
Consistency, right? Remind myself of that.

00:05:25.211 --> 00:05:28.236
Watching videos that are
positive and uplifting,

00:05:28.236 --> 00:05:31.155
and how CEOs, and
entrepreneurs, and athletes

00:05:31.155 --> 00:05:32.796
are dealing with all
these negative situations

00:05:32.796 --> 00:05:35.524
makes me feel more positive.

00:05:35.524 --> 00:05:37.048
And so designing your environment

00:05:37.048 --> 00:05:38.422
and your morning routine

00:05:38.422 --> 00:05:41.505
so that you just fall into that daily

00:05:42.755 --> 00:05:46.667
helps you start to reframe
your thought process.

00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:47.996
So what I don't want you to do

00:05:47.996 --> 00:05:49.892
is wake up every day
and not know what to do,

00:05:49.892 --> 00:05:52.270
or just fall into a pattern
that doesn't support you,

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:53.916
that isn't intentional.

00:05:53.916 --> 00:05:54.970
Where if you spend some time,

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.351
and spend a day on a Sunday afternoon,

00:05:56.351 --> 00:05:58.707
think, how did I want my
schedule to look like?

00:05:58.707 --> 00:06:01.517
What does a morning
routine look like for me

00:06:01.517 --> 00:06:03.112
that will allow me to be more positive

00:06:03.112 --> 00:06:05.392
and eliminate negativity from my life?

00:06:05.392 --> 00:06:07.418
And when I am faced with negativity,

00:06:07.418 --> 00:06:08.692
I'll have the tools to fight it.

00:06:08.692 --> 00:06:10.189
What does that morning routine look like?

00:06:10.189 --> 00:06:12.343
And with intention, create it,

00:06:12.343 --> 00:06:14.070
and then follow it, every day.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:15.364
Like I want to wake up every day

00:06:15.364 --> 00:06:16.442
and just follow my routine.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.894
I don't have to think
first thing in the morning.

00:06:17.894 --> 00:06:19.311
I just fall into my routine

00:06:19.311 --> 00:06:21.570
and I took the time to create a routine

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:23.072
that supports the belief system

00:06:23.072 --> 00:06:24.143
that I'm trying to build.

00:06:24.143 --> 00:06:27.177
(upbeat music)

00:06:27.177 --> 00:06:28.805
- Tip number four is pay
attention to the words

00:06:28.805 --> 00:06:30.177
that you use.

00:06:30.177 --> 00:06:32.192
The words that you use
to describe situations

00:06:32.192 --> 00:06:34.162
will often create the emotions

00:06:34.162 --> 00:06:36.328
that can follow you throughout the day.

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:38.608
So watch out for the words that you use.

00:06:38.608 --> 00:06:40.856
I've been personally
working on this a lot,

00:06:40.856 --> 00:06:42.494
so when an annoying situation happens,

00:06:42.494 --> 00:06:44.150
whether it's a customer that's not happy

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:45.627
or I'm stuck in traffic,

00:06:45.627 --> 00:06:47.532
you know, it comes over you like, ah!

00:06:47.532 --> 00:06:49.180
I can't believe this is happening!

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.992
You say dammit, shoot, drop the f-bomb,

00:06:51.992 --> 00:06:54.601
so many things that you
can just throw out there

00:06:54.601 --> 00:06:56.540
when something annoying comes your way.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:59.479
But here's the thing,
emotion on a chemical level

00:06:59.479 --> 00:07:03.584
can last anywhere from a few
seconds up to 90 seconds.

00:07:03.584 --> 00:07:07.312
After that, it's often
the labels that you put.

00:07:07.312 --> 00:07:09.395
So here's what I'm doing.

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:12.044
Any time something really
frustrating happens,

00:07:12.044 --> 00:07:14.750
I label it as, it's a pickle,

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.357
and how do I solve it?

00:07:16.357 --> 00:07:18.104
Just me saying that it's a pickle,

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:20.330
no matter how bad it is,

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:22.818
first of all cracks me up, makes me laugh,

00:07:22.818 --> 00:07:25.454
and really at the end of it makes me focus

00:07:25.454 --> 00:07:27.809
on how do I solve this thing.

00:07:27.809 --> 00:07:29.630
And really, labeling it like that

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.368
makes it more manageable for me.

00:07:31.368 --> 00:07:33.134
So what I want you to do is

00:07:33.134 --> 00:07:34.981
pay attention to the words that you use

00:07:34.981 --> 00:07:38.162
any time something difficult
or annoying happens.

00:07:38.162 --> 00:07:39.862
Are you cursing?

00:07:39.862 --> 00:07:43.455
Are you just physically
just really turning red

00:07:43.455 --> 00:07:45.930
and yelling at your dog?

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:46.862
I hope not.

00:07:46.862 --> 00:07:48.083
(laughs)

00:07:48.083 --> 00:07:51.011
But it's important that you pay attention

00:07:51.011 --> 00:07:52.129
to the words that you use.

00:07:52.129 --> 00:07:53.697
They have a lot of power.

00:07:53.697 --> 00:07:55.326
So next time something annoying happens,

00:07:55.326 --> 00:07:57.095
pay attention to the words you use

00:07:57.095 --> 00:07:58.470
and change them,

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.269
because once you change
the words that you use

00:08:00.269 --> 00:08:03.279
and the labels that you
place on your environment,

00:08:03.279 --> 00:08:07.213
you can either become more
positive or more negative.

00:08:07.213 --> 00:08:09.796
(upbeat music)

00:08:10.837 --> 00:08:11.893
- Number five is model success.

00:08:11.893 --> 00:08:13.210
I love model success.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:15.227
It's one of my go-tos always
when I'm trying to figure out

00:08:15.227 --> 00:08:17.063
how to do something that I
don't know what to do with.

00:08:17.063 --> 00:08:18.951
One of the things that
I always remind myself

00:08:18.951 --> 00:08:20.795
with this negative positive thing is,

00:08:20.795 --> 00:08:22.807
there's people who have
way worse situations.

00:08:22.807 --> 00:08:24.909
Like I'm actually really
blessed with a fortune,

00:08:24.909 --> 00:08:26.058
and so are you.

00:08:26.058 --> 00:08:27.466
When you think about
where you're at in life,

00:08:27.466 --> 00:08:28.550
the fact that we have a computer,

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:29.383
you have internet,

00:08:29.383 --> 00:08:30.535
you can watch this video,

00:08:30.535 --> 00:08:31.920
you're ahead of most people in the world,

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.166
and there's a lot of people.

00:08:33.166 --> 00:08:35.556
Some of your heroes,
people you look up to,

00:08:35.556 --> 00:08:38.560
who have way less than what
you already have right now,

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:40.539
surrounding myself with those stories

00:08:40.539 --> 00:08:42.566
consistently helps me remember that

00:08:42.566 --> 00:08:45.545
they were able to do it with a lot less

00:08:45.545 --> 00:08:46.662
than what I have now.

00:08:46.662 --> 00:08:47.648
I can do it, too.

00:08:47.648 --> 00:08:49.755
They serve both as tactical, right,

00:08:49.755 --> 00:08:50.797
like here's what you can do,

00:08:50.797 --> 00:08:52.216
here's how they did it,

00:08:52.216 --> 00:08:54.192
but also motivational, inspirational,

00:08:54.192 --> 00:08:56.889
because by following their stories,

00:08:56.889 --> 00:08:58.735
just by understanding that these people

00:08:58.735 --> 00:09:01.535
grew up with such bad family situations,

00:09:01.535 --> 00:09:04.607
such poor resources, such limited access

00:09:04.607 --> 00:09:06.234
to everything, and made it out

00:09:06.234 --> 00:09:07.769
and built these amazing businesses

00:09:07.769 --> 00:09:09.270
and had these insane careers,

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:11.713
watching that helps me.

00:09:11.713 --> 00:09:14.741
And early on in my career, before YouTube,

00:09:14.741 --> 00:09:16.210
it was a book. I was reading books

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.619
of successful entrepreneurs,

00:09:17.619 --> 00:09:20.178
and there was this one book that had

00:09:20.178 --> 00:09:21.430
a couple pages per entrepreneur.

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:22.617
I would read one every day.

00:09:22.617 --> 00:09:24.660
Just not read a whole
book, just a couple pages.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.845
You have time to read three,
four pages on a person.

00:09:26.845 --> 00:09:28.934
And again, it gave me
the motivational boost,

00:09:28.934 --> 00:09:30.947
the inspirational boost
as well as tactics,

00:09:30.947 --> 00:09:33.018
and now I use them in videos, right?

00:09:33.018 --> 00:09:34.967
By seeing these successful
people come from nothing

00:09:34.967 --> 00:09:36.447
and have to deal with so much,

00:09:36.447 --> 00:09:38.681
I think, I'm complaining about this stuff

00:09:38.681 --> 00:09:40.962
where these people have
done such amazing things

00:09:40.962 --> 00:09:43.673
that had to deal with all
of that in their lives?

00:09:43.673 --> 00:09:47.359
So having that really helped
me be able to overcome it,

00:09:47.359 --> 00:09:48.600
and if you model success,

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:50.234
find the people who've gone through

00:09:50.234 --> 00:09:52.452
what it is that you are going through

00:09:52.452 --> 00:09:54.504
and come out the other side,

00:09:54.504 --> 00:09:56.129
both from inspiration and from tactics,

00:09:56.129 --> 00:09:57.996
it'll help you accomplish
your goal, as well.

00:09:57.996 --> 00:10:01.099
(upbeat music)

00:10:01.099 --> 00:10:03.424
Tip number six is having
an accountability partner.

00:10:03.424 --> 00:10:04.902
I find it really helpful

00:10:04.902 --> 00:10:06.896
when you're trying to follow
through on a new habit

00:10:06.896 --> 00:10:08.488
to have somebody in your life

00:10:08.488 --> 00:10:10.073
who holds you accountable,

00:10:10.073 --> 00:10:11.345
who says, hey, you're not doing the thing

00:10:11.345 --> 00:10:12.580
that you said you were going to do.

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:14.925
You know, you asked me
to keep you accountable,

00:10:14.925 --> 00:10:16.258
and you're not doing the thing

00:10:16.258 --> 00:10:17.628
that you said was important to you.

00:10:17.628 --> 00:10:19.538
I find that, that's really important,

00:10:19.538 --> 00:10:20.974
because we will let ourselves down

00:10:20.974 --> 00:10:22.810
more than we'll let other people down,

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:24.415
and sometimes we need a reminder.

00:10:24.415 --> 00:10:26.373
And so if I look at my habit of the,

00:10:26.373 --> 00:10:28.269
there's no such thing as a bad day.

00:10:28.269 --> 00:10:30.237
I told Dina, I told my wife,

00:10:30.237 --> 00:10:32.413
say, hey Dina, if you hear me complaining

00:10:32.413 --> 00:10:34.342
about something negative,

00:10:34.342 --> 00:10:35.828
I want you to remind me that

00:10:35.828 --> 00:10:37.561
there's no such thing as a bad day.

00:10:37.561 --> 00:10:39.311
And when she does, it's
like, ugh, you're right,

00:10:39.311 --> 00:10:41.514
yeah, you're right, okay, okay, okay,

00:10:41.514 --> 00:10:42.467
and I try to adjust.

00:10:42.467 --> 00:10:44.456
But like, that's the process.

00:10:44.456 --> 00:10:47.094
It's catching the
negativity in the moment.

00:10:47.094 --> 00:10:48.529
I tell people on my team,

00:10:48.529 --> 00:10:50.208
you're team yes, I told (mumbles),

00:10:50.208 --> 00:10:51.041
I told Lily,

00:10:51.041 --> 00:10:51.874
just knocked the second book over.

00:10:51.874 --> 00:10:53.478
There's no such thing as a bad day.

00:10:53.478 --> 00:10:55.608
I told them on my team, said, hey listen,

00:10:55.608 --> 00:10:57.715
if you, I'm trying to build this habit

00:10:57.715 --> 00:10:59.484
there's no such thing as a bad day.

00:10:59.484 --> 00:11:01.444
If you find me falling off track,

00:11:01.444 --> 00:11:03.058
I want you to catch me.

00:11:03.058 --> 00:11:04.188
And their default reaction was like,

00:11:04.188 --> 00:11:05.048
you're always positive.

00:11:05.048 --> 00:11:06.113
You don't complain about stuff.

00:11:06.113 --> 00:11:07.983
It's like, I know, that's great.

00:11:07.983 --> 00:11:10.246
You know, my, I'm 95% positive,

00:11:10.246 --> 00:11:12.827
but that 5% when I might be complaining,

00:11:12.827 --> 00:11:13.704
I might be upset,

00:11:13.704 --> 00:11:15.254
you know, just remind me,

00:11:15.254 --> 00:11:16.087
there's no such thing as a bad day.

00:11:16.087 --> 00:11:17.613
So having people to hold me accountable

00:11:17.613 --> 00:11:19.196
when I forget, when I lapse,

00:11:19.196 --> 00:11:21.955
you know, and it's something
that I say is important to me.

00:11:21.955 --> 00:11:24.018
And so some people may be afraid to

00:11:24.018 --> 00:11:25.714
find the people in your life who,

00:11:25.714 --> 00:11:27.462
you know, will stand up to you and say,

00:11:27.462 --> 00:11:28.932
listen, I'm only doing this because

00:11:28.932 --> 00:11:30.881
you told me to do this,
those kind of people,

00:11:30.881 --> 00:11:32.426
I think is important.

00:11:32.426 --> 00:11:34.035
When you commit to somebody else,

00:11:34.035 --> 00:11:36.045
when you have somebody else
to hold you accountable,

00:11:36.045 --> 00:11:38.494
you're much more likely to
follow through with anything.

00:11:38.494 --> 00:11:41.843
(upbeat music)

00:11:41.843 --> 00:11:44.425
And tip number seven is
remember your one word.

00:11:44.425 --> 00:11:46.306
I should put the books back up.

00:11:46.306 --> 00:11:48.525
If we're talking about your one word,

00:11:48.525 --> 00:11:50.292
we've got to have the books.

00:11:50.292 --> 00:11:52.058
It kind of makes sense, right?

00:11:52.058 --> 00:11:53.558
Stay. Stay, books.

00:11:54.783 --> 00:11:57.144
When you know, when you
have the self awareness

00:11:57.144 --> 00:11:58.759
to know what it is that you stand for,

00:11:58.759 --> 00:12:00.139
right, what your one word is,

00:12:00.139 --> 00:12:02.539
what the most important
core value is in your life,

00:12:02.539 --> 00:12:05.159
then it's much more easy to
stay on the positive track

00:12:05.159 --> 00:12:07.864
because you want to, for
me it's believe, right?

00:12:07.864 --> 00:12:08.889
I want to believe more.

00:12:08.889 --> 00:12:09.799
I want to believe in myself.

00:12:09.799 --> 00:12:11.374
I want to believe in other people more.

00:12:11.374 --> 00:12:13.891
And your one word is always
something positive, right?

00:12:13.891 --> 00:12:16.134
I've never had somebody
who's one word was negative,

00:12:16.134 --> 00:12:20.086
who's one word was hate
or kill or destroy.

00:12:20.086 --> 00:12:22.190
It's always something positive.

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:24.296
And so it's an easy way to get back

00:12:24.296 --> 00:12:27.213
to the positive spot inside of you.

00:12:28.389 --> 00:12:29.892
So if you're designing your environment

00:12:29.892 --> 00:12:31.616
around, so for me, believe, right,

00:12:31.616 --> 00:12:33.156
or just reminding yourself when you're

00:12:33.156 --> 00:12:34.558
reading your credo on a daily basis

00:12:34.558 --> 00:12:37.291
or creating an environment
that is your one word for you,

00:12:37.291 --> 00:12:39.759
I want believe to be everywhere around me.

00:12:39.759 --> 00:12:41.237
My office, when I walk in, is believe.

00:12:41.237 --> 00:12:43.615
My videos are believe, they ooze believe.

00:12:43.615 --> 00:12:45.472
The content I make is around believe.

00:12:45.472 --> 00:12:46.952
The things that I feed my head in, with,

00:12:46.952 --> 00:12:48.604
is around believe.

00:12:48.604 --> 00:12:49.597
It's important.

00:12:49.597 --> 00:12:51.713
So when you can design your
environment, your routine,

00:12:51.713 --> 00:12:54.002
and everything you absorb on a daily basis

00:12:54.002 --> 00:12:56.684
around your one word, that
most important core value

00:12:56.684 --> 00:12:57.881
that makes you feel great,

00:12:57.881 --> 00:13:00.190
you're much more likely to stay positive.

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.572
So that's my take on the seven ways

00:13:01.572 --> 00:13:03.139
to stop your negative thinking.

00:13:03.139 --> 00:13:05.514
I made this video because
Amarin Winino asked me to,

00:13:05.514 --> 00:13:07.592
so if there's a topic you'd like mt cover

00:13:07.592 --> 00:13:09.074
in a future seven ways video,

00:13:09.074 --> 00:13:10.736
check out the link in the description,

00:13:10.736 --> 00:13:12.421
and you can go and cast your vote.

00:13:12.421 --> 00:13:14.469
I'd also love to know what
did you think of this video,

00:13:14.469 --> 00:13:16.996
which one was the most
important point for you,

00:13:16.996 --> 00:13:18.816
how are you going to stop
your negative thinking.

00:13:18.816 --> 00:13:20.893
Did I miss an eight, nine,
10 that you want to add

00:13:20.893 --> 00:13:22.087
to the list?

00:13:22.087 --> 00:13:23.368
Leave your thoughts in the comments below,

00:13:23.368 --> 00:13:25.023
and I'm excited to see
what you guys have to say.

00:13:25.023 --> 00:13:27.247
I also want to give a quick shout out

